{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nOn 2026-09-01 the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on `rebar-gerrit` fail-closed reviews because root disk reached 91-95%; review clones/materializations hit ENOSPC and surfaced as `coverage-gap (review-error)`. Change 2481 exhausted its retry budget to a spurious LLM-Review -1. Recovery required manual `docker builder prune -f` without `--keep-storage`, proving automated prune could not reclaim below its 5GB build-cache floor. Operator approved implementing fixes A+B.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` always runs `docker builder prune -f --keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"`, even on acute pressure/no-op tick paths. At 5.244GB cache, automated prune freed ~0.\n2. The review hot path starts clones/materializations without checking free disk first. `voter.py` clones into `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")` on the root temp volume; `repo_snapshot.py` materializes into the snapshot-store volume.\n\n## Approved implementation plan\n\n### A. Acute pressure reclaim tier\n\nKeep normal warm-cache behavior unchanged. Add `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT` default 90, above soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT=80`. When root used-% is at/above hard threshold, `prune_docker_caches()` escalates BuildKit reclaim to `docker builder prune -f` with keep->0 (no `--keep-storage`), best-effort/non-fatal and `timeout 120` bounded like existing docker calls. Measure before/after root filesystem bytes and log bytes actually freed; success evidence is `bytes_freed > 0`, not invocation.\n\n### B. Low-disk admission control\n\nAdd target-path free-space helper in `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py` (`shutil.disk_usage(path)`) and `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` default 2. This is a hard pre-clone admission floor; existing janitor watermarks remain cleanup targets.\n\nCheck target volume before cloning/materializing:\n\n- In `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`, before `TemporaryDirectory` / `gc.clone_change_ref`, measure `tempfile.gettempdir()`.\n- In `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` / `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py`, measure the snapshot-store path before attested snapshot clone/materialize.\n\nRepresent low disk explicitly. Snapshot admission raises a dedicated `LowDiskError` (or returns an equivalent low-disk sentinel) with target path/free/floor. `gate_source.py` maps that condition into structured coverage as `coverage[\"low_disk\"] = True` and preserves details; `adapter._coverage_gap_reason` gains a first branch `if coverage.get(\"low_disk\"): return \"low-disk\"`. Do not let low disk fall through to generic `review-error`.\n\nFor the Gerrit voter pre-clone guard, synthesize a decision with `verdict=\"BLOCK\"`, `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`, and first line `[LLM-Review: BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)] ...`. Define `_TAG_SUFFIXES[\"low-disk\"] = \"BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)\"`; add `low-disk` to `adapter.RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS`; keep `retrigger.py` parsing the existing `coverage-gap (<reason>)` grammar.\n\nIn `_handle_retryable_gap`, add explicit low-disk semantics. Under budget it defers vote-less like existing ADR 0069 retryable gaps. At/over the low-disk budget it returns `deferred_result` with a terminal status such as `deferred-exhausted`, `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`, writes/logs an operator-visible neutral Gerrit comment/status explaining low disk exhausted retry holdback and that a `recheck`/new patchset will retry after disk remediation, but leaves labels unchanged: no `LLM-Review -1`, no `append_retries_exhausted_note`, no `VOTER_ERROR`. This converges safely by making the change non-submittable due to missing LLM vote while avoiding a false code veto; explicit recheck/new patchset remains the recovery path after the host is healthy. Existing exhaustion behavior for non-low-disk review errors/coverage gaps is unchanged. Document in ADR 0069, ADR 0077, `docs/review-policy.md`, and `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Hard-pressure reclaim: root used-% >= `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT` with enough reclaimable build-cache excess causes emergency keep->0 builder prune, logs/measures `bytes_freed > 0`, and fixture returns below soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT`; proof in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py` and/or `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`.\n- [ ] Warm-cache regression: below `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT`, `prune_docker_caches()` still uses `--keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"`; proof in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py`.\n- [ ] Review-bot low-disk admission: below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` on `tempfile.gettempdir()`, `voter.py` does not create the clone and defers retryably/vote-less through ADR 0069; proof by focused voter test asserting no clone/vote.\n- [ ] Exhausted low-disk budget: labels remain unchanged/no `LLM-Review -1`, with a neutral operator-visible exhausted-deferral result recoverable by recheck/new patchset; proof contrasts `low-disk` with `review-error` exhaustion.\n- [ ] Snapshot low-disk admission: below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` on the snapshot-store volume, materialization aborts before clone with `coverage[\"low_disk\"]` -> `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`; proof around `repo_snapshot.py` / `gate_source.py` / adapter coverage routing.\n- [ ] Distinct semantics: literal suffix `BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)` and routing tests distinguish low-disk from genuine coverage/review errors.\n- [ ] Portability: all reclaim/admission logic is in-process/operation-linked, with no CI-provider dependency.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest <focused low-disk review admission/voter tests> -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\n## File impact\n\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`; `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py`; `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py`; `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`; `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`; `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py`; `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py`; `docs/review-policy.md`; `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`; `docs/adr/0069-retryable-coverage-gap-bounded-deferral.md`; `docs/adr/0077-code-review-voter-four-pass-rewire.md`; focused tests."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788311408386011478,"uuid":"a28f94d4-53c5-4a87-9e8e-394c83404f0f"}